\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $d,k\geq 1$ and measurable partition $A_{1},\dots ,A_k$ of $R^{d}$, must $\Sigma _i\Vert \int _{A_i}x$ $d\gamma _d(x)\Vert ^{2}\leq 9/(8\pi )$, where $\gamma _d$ is standard Gaussian probability? Empty cells and arbitrary cell masses are allowed. For $d\geq 2,k\geq 3$, is the bound attained by three planar sectors of angle $2\pi /3$ times their orthogonal complement, with remaining cells empty?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $d,k\geq 1$ and measurable partition $A_{1},\dots ,A_k$ of $R^{d}$, must $\Sigma _i\Vert \int _{A_i}x$ $d\gamma _d(x)\Vert ^{2}\leq 9/(8\pi )$, where $\gamma _d$ is standard Gaussian probability? Empty cells and arbitrary cell masses are allowed. For $d\geq 2,k\geq 3$, is the bound attained by three planar sectors of angle $2\pi /3$ times their orthogonal complement, with remaining cells empty?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

